WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.316 --> 00:00:02.668
(whizzing)
(door hinge)

00:00:02.753 --> 00:00:03.775
- Warm days, am I right?

00:00:03.835 --> 00:00:05.021
- Oh, you're tellin' me.

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:07.465
Ey, how's the old lady, huh?

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:09.955
- Ey, which one? My wife or my neighbor?

00:00:09.955 --> 00:00:11.123
- Ahh!

00:00:11.123 --> 00:00:12.453
- Ey you know, so what about yourself?

00:00:12.453 --> 00:00:16.052
- Met this nice little
waitress down at the Denny's.

00:00:16.052 --> 00:00:17.074
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:17.074 --> 00:00:18.038
Her name's Maria.

00:00:18.038 --> 00:00:19.512
- You gotta be careful
Becky doesn't find out.

00:00:19.512 --> 00:00:21.474
- Oh, no, Becky doesn't know a thing.

00:00:21.474 --> 00:00:21.913
(phone vibrating)

00:00:21.913 --> 00:00:23.309
Hold on, I'm gettin' a phone call here.

00:00:23.309 --> 00:00:23.679
- Okay.

00:00:23.679 --> 00:00:24.269
(clears throat)

00:00:24.829 --> 00:00:25.714
Hello?

00:00:26.463 --> 00:00:28.012
Free dozen roses, you say?

00:00:28.388 --> 00:00:30.919
Yo, Jeff. This company's
sayin' they wanna give me

00:00:30.919 --> 00:00:34.045
a free dozen roses to
send to anyone I want.

00:00:34.045 --> 00:00:35.566
All I have to do is give 'em a first name.

00:00:35.566 --> 00:00:37.905
How 'bout that waitress down at Denny's?

00:00:38.608 --> 00:00:40.763
- I hate to break it to
you, sounds like a scam.

00:00:40.763 --> 00:00:42.218
I think you're on a radio show, buddy.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.325
- I'm sorry, radio show?

00:00:44.325 --> 00:00:46.265
- You know, a radio show
where a wife calls in

00:00:46.265 --> 00:00:47.843
suspecting a husband's cheating.

00:00:47.843 --> 00:00:49.781
Then they call him up,
offer him a dozen roses.

00:00:49.781 --> 00:00:51.581
If he picks his side chick over her,

00:00:51.581 --> 00:00:53.079
they call him out on it.

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:54.158
Dude, I think you're gettin' set up.

00:00:54.158 --> 00:00:56.376
- Yeah, Jeff. All they
need is a first name.

00:00:56.376 --> 00:00:58.859
No last name, no street address,

00:00:58.859 --> 00:01:01.014
no billin' info, nothin'.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.703
They'll find her on their own.

00:01:02.703 --> 00:01:03.816
How crazy is that?

00:01:03.816 --> 00:01:06.116
- You're tellin' me some flower business

00:01:06.116 --> 00:01:09.285
is gonna be able to track down
a woman by her first name?

00:01:09.285 --> 00:01:10.700
What is this? The CIA?

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.221
- You know the technology these
days and Twitter, who knows?

00:01:13.221 --> 00:01:14.939
- I don't know, I'mma just
tell you one more time,

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:16.611
I think you're on a morning radio show.

00:01:16.611 --> 00:01:19.684
- Listen Jeff, I'm not on a radio show.

00:01:19.684 --> 00:01:22.304
- [Radio] "Listen Jeff,
I'm not on a radio show."

00:01:22.958 --> 00:01:24.444
- I mean, what else do you want?

00:01:24.444 --> 00:01:26.661
- I.. I think that's a coincidence.

00:01:27.232 --> 00:01:28.741
- [Radio] I think that's a coincidence.

00:01:28.741 --> 00:01:29.903
- Ey, listen Jeff. Can
you turn that down Jeff?

00:01:29.903 --> 00:01:31.051
That's kinda echoing here.

00:01:31.051 --> 00:01:33.768
They just upped it to 53 roses, Jeff.

00:01:33.768 --> 00:01:35.742
How could I turn down the deal, huh?

00:01:35.742 --> 00:01:36.729
- I'm gonna tell you right now.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:40.629
You are 100% definitely
on a radio show right now.

00:01:40.629 --> 00:01:41.942
- You've been listenin' to too much radio.

00:01:41.942 --> 00:01:44.030
I shoulda never given you
that thing for Christmas.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:44.611
- You know what?

00:01:44.611 --> 00:01:46.132
If you actually think you're
gonna get away with it,

00:01:46.132 --> 00:01:46.666
go for it.

00:01:46.666 --> 00:01:48.555
- Yeah, I do. I do. You know what Jeff?

00:01:48.555 --> 00:01:50.906
I'm gonna tell her a name,
and the name is Maria.

00:01:50.906 --> 00:01:52.625
And I want you to include a note,

00:01:52.625 --> 00:01:55.174
"Ey, baby. Miss ya, can't
wait to see ya this weekend."

00:01:56.391 --> 00:01:57.861
Becky, how'd you get on the line?

00:01:58.006 --> 00:01:59.131
- I told you how she got on the line.

00:01:59.528 --> 00:02:01.630
- Oh my God, this is a radio show.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:03.194
- I told you you were on a radio show.

00:02:05.323 --> 00:02:06.228
I'll let ya know right now.

00:02:06.228 --> 00:02:07.836
You just can't, you
can't trust those things.

00:02:07.836 --> 00:02:09.628
It's too good, it's too good to be true.

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:10.426
(phone buzzing)

00:02:10.426 --> 00:02:12.497
- Oh, hold on, gettin' a phone call.

00:02:12.497 --> 00:02:14.808
Hello? Wow.

00:02:15.958 --> 00:02:17.654
I just got offered a free cruise.

00:02:17.654 --> 00:02:20.680
All I have to say is if I'mma
take my wife or my neighbor.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:21.901
- Pfft.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.781
- Yeah, I think her name's Carol.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.727
(upbeat dance music)

00:02:28.912 --> 00:02:30.818
(whizzing)
(door hinge)

